# Pump encoding, GFO (pins: Onto-Med/GFO @ 233b38d, gfo-base module).
#
# R1: the typed parthood suite. gfo-base ships part_of with typed
# refinements; a material component is asserted by the apt refinement,
# constituent_part_of, and the artifact's own hierarchy
# (constituent_part_of < proper_part_of < part_of, the upper two
# transitive) returns the generic parthoods in the closure.
#
# Declarations repeat the pinned artifact's typing so the file renders
# correctly on its own (in Protege, undeclared properties display as
# annotations); semantics -- the property hierarchy, transitivity --
# come only from gfo-base.owl at the pin.
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix gfob: <https://w3id.org/gfo/base/> .
@prefix p:    <https://example.org/mt-pump#> .

gfob:Presential a owl:Class .
gfob:constituent_part_of a owl:ObjectProperty .

p:impeller a gfob:Presential ;
    gfob:constituent_part_of p:pump .
p:pump a gfob:Presential .

# R2: the impeller-housing joint is inexpressible at this layer. The
# theory defines boundary coincidence (the two-level doctrine), but the
# artifact ships no connection or coincidence relation; the front page
# names coincidence among the outstanding features, and no artifact
# vocabulary can state it.
